# Independent goroutine fan-out: WaitGroup, not errgroup

Never use `errgroup.Go` for concurrent operations that must **all** complete regardless of individual failures. `errgroup` cancels remaining goroutines as soon as the first one returns an error.

Use `sync.WaitGroup` with a per-goroutine error slot so each goroutine runs to completion independently.

```go
// ❌ BAD — first error cancels context and may abort remaining goroutines
g, ctx := errgroup.WithContext(ctx)
for _, id := range ids {
    id := id
    g.Go(func() error { return deleteGIF(ctx, id) })
}
return g.Wait()

// ✅ GOOD — each goroutine settles independently; all run to completion
errs := make([]error, len(ids))
var wg sync.WaitGroup
for i, id := range ids {
    i, id := i, id
    wg.Add(1)
    go func() {
        defer wg.Done()
        errs[i] = deleteGIF(ctx, id)
    }()
}
wg.Wait()
// inspect errs[] — some may be non-nil, others nil
```

Use `errgroup` only when a failure in one goroutine should legitimately cancel the others (e.g. a coordinated pipeline where subsequent steps depend on earlier ones succeeding).
